# =============================================================================
# Build context filter for the images built FROM THE REPOSITORY ROOT.
#
# Only `backup-runner` uses the root as its build context, because it has to
# copy scripts/backup/*.sh into the image and the CDC (§10.1) puts those
# scripts under scripts/, not under images/. Every other image has its own
# directory as context and is unaffected by this file — Docker resolves
# .dockerignore relative to the context directory.
#
# The rule is deny-by-default, and that is the point: `secrets/`, `.env`, the
# TLS private keys under `certs/` and the whole git history all live at the
# root. A permissive context would ship them into an image layer, push them to
# the registry, and there is no taking that back.
#
# To add a file to the backup-runner image, allow-list it explicitly below.
# =============================================================================

# Deny everything…
*

# …then allow exactly what the image needs.
!scripts/backup

# Belt and braces: even if the deny-all above is ever relaxed, these must never
# reach a build context.
secrets/
certs/
.env
.git/
